    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 3.6,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings rise exponentially until 5 h and then sit flat at about 0.93–0.96 from 5 to 18 h. That flat line is what a saturated reader would give. The retained 18 h aliquot, diluted 10-fold, read 0.3616. If the undiluted reading were proportional, it would have read about 0.095. Scaled back up, the 10-fold reading corresponds to about 3.6 OD, roughly 4 times the undiluted 0.95. So the undiluted reader is nonlinear at high density and underestimates the late biomass. This rests on a single dilution at 18 h, and the 3.6 figure is only a lower-bound-style estimate, because the 10-fold reading of 0.36 may itself be slightly compressed."
  },
